      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Bucephalandrapygmaea'BukitKelam'(139CLP)/31143",
      "html": "<p>In nature, Bucephalandra usually grows on rocks or wood in rivers and streams - much like Anubias, which they resemble regarding use and care in the aquarium. Bucephalandra 'Wavy Green' is an easy, slow-growing plant that prefers lower light levels. A nice, dense appearance is ensured by the willingness to branch, even without trimming.</p><p>The creeping stem, rhizome, must not be covered when planting. This will cause the plant to rot and die.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Bucephalandrapygmaea'BukitKelam'(139CLP)/31143",
      "html": "<p>The green leaves are 2 cm wide and 5 cm long with wavy edges. Tiny white spots will appear on immersed leaves.</p>"
    }
